<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss bond market closing report.</title>
<headline>Swiss bond market closing report.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss bonds ended Monday higher in quiet trade before the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting on Tuesday, and the Bundesbank's first meeting after its summer recess on Thursday.</p>
<p>The market was also nervous after a selloff in U.S. stocks on Friday followed by early selling in European stocks Monday.</p>
<p>Conf futures up 17 basis points at 119.97.</p>
<p>Euro Swiss francs steady at 98.42.</p>
<p>4-1/2 Jun 2007 bond 108.15/25 yield 3.49 pct</p>
<p>(Friday 108.05/15 yield 3.502 pct)</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
